    "created_at": "2019-11-15T10:59:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-15T10:59:49Z",
    "body": "If you are using zsh, you can follow [this troubleshooting guide](https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/blob/master/README.md#why-is-my-cursor-in-the-wrong-place). It's written for a different theme but most problems that cause the cursor to be in the wrong place are not theme-specific.\r\n\r\nThe very first paragraph diagnoses the problem in most cases:\r\n\r\n>  Type `echo '\\u276F'`. If you get an error saying \"zsh: character not in range\", your locale doesn't support UTF-8. You need to fix it. If you are running zsh over SSH, see [this](https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/issues/153#issuecomment-518347833). If you are running zsh locally, Google \"set UTF-8 locale in *your OS*\".",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
